                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Beauty Bounce is actually better than the original game, with a more fair price for such little content. It’s a full fan service visual novel that doesn’t try to be “deep” or anything, it was made to be like this.\n\nThe same problem that happened with the previous game is still here, where Tomo’s sprite is just a shadow, but we SEE his f*cking face and body on CGs. There’s no point on doing this if the reader already knows how he looks like. It became annoying, to be honest.\n\nBGM was okay, nothing memorable. The girls from the first game are back, and there are some new faces too. Overall, it’s an okay title if you enjoy lots of fan service. Even so, I recommend getting this title on a sale since I was able to finish the whole game in around one hour (I have 3 hours of gameplay registered because I was getting the cards). \n\n5/10.",
